## Overview — Individualized Resection

- Technical refinements have facilitated a **more individualized, disease-directed approach** for patients undergoing pancreatectomy.
- The chapter focuses on:
  - Surgical techniques
  - Pertinent perioperative considerations
- Patient population: those subjected to **open distal and central pancreatectomy**

## Overview — What the Chapter Details

The section details approach, exposure, and technical nuances that facilitate **safe and effective surgical resection** of lesions located in the:

- **Neck** of the pancreas
- **Body** of the pancreas
- **Tail** of the pancreas

## Overview — Related Content (Not Covered Here)

Previous chapters have outlined the definition, classifications, pathogenesis, clinical aspects, diagnostic assessment, and management of:

- Acute pancreatitis
- Chronic pancreatitis
- Periampullary and pancreatic tumors
  - Pancreatic cancer
  - Cystic tumors
  - Endocrine tumors

